          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4sj",
          "text": "In Colorado, an individual may be eligible for financial compensation if an amputation injury was the result of another person’s negligence. Negligence, a legal doctrine, is the basis for most personal injury cases. It refers to someone who acts with a substandard level of care. Proving negligence in an amputation injury case requires evidence of four elements:",
