      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4u2",
          "text": "What Will an Amputation Injury Lawyer Do for Your Case?",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4u5",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4u4",
          "text": "Working with a skilled attorney can be invaluable during an amputation injury case. Your lawyer can protect your legal rights by taking over negotiations with an insurance company for you, ensuring the carrier treats you fairly. Your lawyer will start by investigating your accident to determine who is at fault. An attorney can go up against one or more parties to pursue maximum compensation for significant losses. This is especially important for an injury as serious as a lost limb since you will need adequate compensation to pay for the injury far into the future. Hiring an attorney can improve your odds of securing the best possible case results.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
